  "slug": "kinetic-learning-interpretable-f729",
  "summary": "Recent cfDNA methylation studies pair read- and fragment-level modeling with explicit error correction, improving recovery of fetal and tumor-derived DNA.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is methylation-informed analysis of cell-free DNA, in which read-level and fragment-level models distinguish biological signal from technical artifact. A first-trimester fetal cfDNA methylome of 26M CpG sites underpins the epiSIFT enrichment model, which raises median fetal fraction from 5.1% to 28.4%. ctDNA-BERT, a Transformer, scores individual bisulfite reads using CpG methylation, nucleotide context and fragment end, with xenograft supervision yielding a frozen scorer. JEEPERS detects and corrects jagged-end-induced methylation errors while preserving duplex integrity. What is new is the joint encoding of methylation, sequence context and fragment-end position at single-read resolution, paired with explicit error correction. The Nanopore direct RNA study is methodologically adjacent: it uses genomic DNA as an in vitro transcription template to create a negative control for modification calling, rather than analyzing cfDNA.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
